  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-10-01T05:12:05.421Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I would like to encourage users to create VRChat accounts. Users who are new to VRChat get confused when I mention \"Steam account\" or \"Oculus account\" versus a 'VRChat account'.\nI felt like seeing the four digits on a nameplate was out of place. I wouldn't mind it on the Social menu, but I believe there should be an \"Unverified\" tag on the nameplate HUD to signify that they haven't made a VRChat account.\nThat way, saying \"your account isn't verified\" or \"unverified user\" might be used more frequently to encourage someone to sign up, and have the freedom to use the VRCSDK, ensure VRChat Plus rites can be applied to their account, and grant them the ability to enable two-factor authentication on signing in.\nPotentially make a loading screen tip to educate those who haven't made an account the benefits of having one.",
